---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Friday: Turkey Day" 
  description="The main Turkey Day feast with koji-marinated turkey"
  currentPage="friday"
>
  <Navigation currentPage="friday" />

  <h1>Friday, November 28th - Turkey Day! 🦃</h1>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Morning: Final Prep (10:00 AM)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Remove turkey from refrigerator</li>
      <li>Let sit at room temperature for 30-60 minutes (optional, helps even cooking)</li>
      <li>Prepare roasting setup: wire rack on sheet pan, small amount of water in bottom</li>
      <li>Set up combustion/predictive thermometer</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Noon: Turkey Goes in Oven (12:00 PM)</h2>

    <h3>Roasting Strategy</h3>
    <p>The turkey has been marinating in shio-koji for 36 hours, then air-dried for 36 hours for crispy skin.</p>

    <h4>Dark Meat (Legs & Thighs)</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Start with turkey legs on rack in oven</li>
      <li>Target internal temp: 185°F (dark meat, long cook)</li>
      <li>Use predictive thermometer to calculate timing</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>White Meat (Breasts)</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Based on leg predictions, add breasts to oven</li>
      <li>Time it so breasts finish around 155°F when legs hit 185°F</li>
      <li>Both should finish around same time</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>1:30 PM: Rest & Make Gravy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Remove turkey pieces to rest (off rack, tent with foil if needed)</li>
      <li>Move roasting pan to stovetop</li>
      <li>Deglaze pan, add turkey stock from Thursday</li>
      <li>Build gravy with hybrid thickener system (roux + potato starch + gelatin + xanthan)</li>
      <li>Season to taste</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>About the Gravy</h3>
    <p>This gravy uses a mix of thickeners for body without heaviness:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Roux</strong>: Traditional flavor base, nutty depth</li>
      <li><strong>Potato starch</strong>: Clean, glossy thickening without pasty texture</li>
      <li><strong>Gelatin</strong>: Body and mouthfeel, that demi-glace elastic glide</li>
      <li><strong>Xanthan gum</strong>: Consistency insurance, prevents breakage or weeping</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>2:00 PM: EAT!</h2>
    <h3>The Complete Feast</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Main</strong>: Koji-marinated roasted turkey (legs and breasts)</li>
      <li><strong>Gravy</strong>: Hybrid-thickener turkey gravy</li>
      <li><strong>Condiment</strong>: Homemade cranberry orange compote</li>
      <li><strong>Sides</strong>:
        <ul>
          <li>Maple-sage Brussels sprouts with sausage and fennel</li>
          <li>Creamy hasselback potatoes au gratin</li>
          <li>Classic brioche stuffing</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>Bread</strong>: Homemade milk bread dinner rolls (reheated from Thursday)</li>
      <li><strong>Desserts</strong>:
        <ul>
          <li>Simple pumpkin pie</li>
          <li>Eggnog Basque cheesecake (from Thursday)</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Why This Works</h2>
    <p>The two-day approach means:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Stock is cold and ready for gravy</li>
      <li>Bread is already baked</li>
      <li>Dessert is set and chilled</li>
      <li>Turkey just needs to roast</li>
      <li>No chaos, just execution</li>
    </ul>

    <p>The koji marinade delivered:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Deep umami flavor (enzymes breaking down proteins)</li>
      <li>Extra tenderness (protein restructuring)</li>
      <li>Better moisture retention</li>
      <li>No need for butter-based brine</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem;">
    <a href="/leftovers" class="btn">Next: Leftovers Pie →</a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

